    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_AboutTab">About</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_AboutDescription">Display Manager applies a Windows display and HDR profile when a game starts and restores the previous desktop state when the game stops — built for HTPC / couch setups in Playnite Desktop and Fullscreen.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_AboutPurposeTitle">What Display Manager does</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_AboutDisplays">Choose which display a game uses, rename monitors with EDID-stable identity, and trial topology changes with automatic restore.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_AboutProfiles">Own HDR with global policies, Features/Tags metadata matching, and per-game overrides. Optional refresh-rate changes restore with the topology snapshot.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_AboutIntegration">Desktop top panel, Theme API for Fullscreen themes, RestoreHost if Playnite exits unexpectedly, and a soft Audio Switcher hook when that extension is installed.</sys:String>
